{{Quote|Those systems are beyond the Outer Rim, in Wild Space. Not on any map.|[[Kanan Jarrus]]|<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" />}}
'''Wild Space''' was a region of [[the galaxy]] that contained uncharted [[planet]]s and [[star]] [[Star cluster|clusters]]. It was located "off the edge of the map" and almost fully unmapped throughout [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]]. In contrast, the [[Unknown Regions]] were mapped but largely unexplored.

The mysterious realm of [[Mortis]] was located in Wild Space, as were the [[planet]]s [[Mulita]], [[Teth]], [[Indoumodo]], [[Kalee]], [[Huk]], [[Thune]], [[Pion]], [[Agaris]], [[Lysatra]], and [[Lira San]], the original [[homeworld]] of the [[Lasat]] [[species]].

==Description==
Wild Space was a large region of unmapped [[star]] clusters<ref name="GalacticAtlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref>  containing dangerous worlds.<ref name="SW VE" /> The [[human]]s of the [[Core Worlds]] often expressed prejudice against [[Sentience|sentient]] beings from Wild Space, even against fellow humans. For example, [[Commandant]] [[Deenlark]] of the [[Royal Imperial Academy]] on [[Coruscant]] discriminated against [[Eli N. Vanto|Eli Vanto]] of [[Lysatra]], whom he termed a "backwater yokel" from Wild Space.<ref name="Thrawn" /> In contrast, the [[Unknown Regions]] were mapped, it was mostly unexplored.<ref name="Rebels Recon 2.14">{{RebelsRecon|cto9_9qNHZ0|#2.14: Inside "The Call" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-the-call}}</ref>

==History==
===Early history===
[[File:Teth_Bomarr_Monastery.png|thumb|left|250px|The B'omarr Monastery on Teth.]]
The [[Lasat]] [[homeworld]] of [[Lira San]] was known to be located in Wild Space. It was separated from the rest of [[the galaxy]] by an imploded [[star cluster]]. The Lasat of Lira San colonized the [[planet]] [[Lasan]] at some point before the [[Imperial Era]]. Eventually, contact between Lira San and Lasan was lost. Those Lasat living on Lasan came to believe that Lira San was a fabled Lasat sanctuary.<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" /> [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]] the [[Hutt]] had his [[Papa|father]] [[Burial|buried]] on the [[jungle]] world of [[Teth]]. Ziro also hid the [[Grand Hutt Council|Hutt Council's]] [[Hutt Council records|records]] with him.<ref name="Hunt for Ziro">{{TCW|Hunt for Ziro}}</ref>

===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Teth? That's Wild Space. The droid army isn't even in that sector.|Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="TCW movie" />|audio=TethWildSpace-TCWf.flac}}
With the [[First Battle of Geonosis|outbreak]] of the [[Clone Wars]], a conflict that pitted the [[Galactic Republic]] against the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], exploration of Wild Space slowed considerably.<ref name="The Escape" /> In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Teth Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the events of the [[Battle of Christophsis]] and the early events of the [[Battle of Ryloth]] to [[22 BBY]]. As the film this event takes place within takes place between the events of the pieces of media the other events are attached to according to {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}}, this event must also take place in 22 BBY.</ref> [[Teth]] hosted a [[B'omarr Order Monastery]], which the Separatist [[assassin]] [[Asajj Ventress]] used to hide [[Rotta]], the kidnapped son of [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]]. Several of Jabba's bounty hunters and a pair of [[Advanced Recon Force trooper|ARF troopers]] tracked Ventress to the Monastery. The clones reported this to [[Jedi General]] [[Mace Windu]], but the bounty hunters were beheaded. As a result, the [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and his new [[Padawan]], [[Ahsoka Tano]], were sent to Teth along with the [[clone trooper]]s of the [[501st Legion|501st's]] [[Torrent Company]] immediately after their [[Battle of Christophsis|victory]] on [[Christophsis]] in order to [[Battle of Teth|rescue]] Rotta.<ref name="TCW movie" /> Around a [[21 BBY|year]] later,<ref name="Ziro Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of "[[ARC Troopers (episode)|ARC Troopers]]" to [[21 BBY]] and the events of "[[Nightsisters (episode)|Nightsisters]]" to [[20 BBY]]. As the episode "[[Hunt for Ziro]]" takes place between the two episodes according to {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}}, Ziro Desilijic Tiure's [[death]] must take place between those two [[Standard year|years]].</ref> Ziro, Jabba's uncle, was [[Death|killed]] there by his estranged former lover [[Sy Snootles]], who retrieved Ziro's stolen Hutt Council records before he could sell it to the Republic.<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" />

Wild Space was also known to be the location of an enigmatic planet called [[Mortis]], which was home to a family of [[Force wielder]]s known as [[Father (Mortis)|the Father]], the [[Daughter]], and the [[Son]]. These three figures embodied the balance in [[the Force]], the [[Light side of the Force|light side]], and the [[dark side of the Force]] respectively. The Force wielders [[Mission to Mortis|tried]] to convince Skywalker to fulfill his prophesied role as the [[Chosen One]].<ref name="Overlords" /> However, their plans were upended when the Son was corrupted by the dark side, setting in motion a chain of events which led to the deaths of the three Force wielders. Their realm existed outside of the realm of normal [[time]] and [[Realspace|space]].<ref name="Ghosts of Mortis">{{TCW|Ghosts of Mortis}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
[[File:The_Ghost_approaches_the_star_cluster.png|thumb|right|250px|The ''Ghost'' approaching a collapsed star cluster]]
During the reign of the [[Galactic Empire]], travelers again traversed Wild Space. The [[New Order|new government's]] [[Imperial Survey Corps|Survey Corps]] even took an interest in the farthest reaches of uncharted space. Demand for maps of Wild Space increased as a consequence, allowing [[cartographer]]s to make a decent living by producing and selling them. [[Auric Graf|Auric]] and [[Rhyssa Graf]], a pair of [[Marriage|married]] interplanetary [[Scout|explorers]], spent fifteen [[Standard year|years]] making maps of Wild Space until their capture by [[Captain]] [[Visler Aqorian Korda III]] of the [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="The Escape" />

Despite the increased interest in Wild Space, those who resided from it were not as well respected by some during this period. [[Eli N. Vanto|Eli Vanto]] and his [[Vanto (Ms.)|mother]] and [[Vanto (Mr.)|father]] came from Wild Space, and Vanto in particular was not well respected for some time, despite his service to the Empire.<ref name="Thrawn" />

In [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Lira San Date">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]'' states that [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] was 16 [[Standard year|years]] old during her [[Mission on Lothal|mission]] on [[Lothal]]. Since ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' establishes that Organa was [[Reproduction|born]] in [[19 BBY]], the mission must take place in [[3 BBY]]. ''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]'' dates the [[Attack on Phoenix Squadron (3 BBY)|attack]] on [[Phoenix Squadron]] to three [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], or [[3 BBY]] according to ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''{{'}} [[Galactic standard calendar|dating system]]. As this rediscovery takes place between these two events, it must also take place in 3 BBY.</ref> the Lasat rebel [[Garazeb Orrelios]], the [[Spectres]] rebel cell, and the Lasat [[refugee]]s [[Chava]] the Wise and [[Gron]] took part in a search for the legendary Lasat sanctuary of Lira San. Lira San lay in Wild Space, and could only be reached by navigating through a collapsed star cluster. After being pursued by [[Imperial Military|Imperial forces]] and a difficult trial, Orrelios managed to used [[AB-75 bo-rifle|his]] [[bo-rifle]] to guide the rebel [[starship]] ''[[Ghost]]'' through the maelstrom. Chava and Gron settled on Lira San, which they [[Rediscovery of Lira San|discovered]] to be the original Lasat homeworld.<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" />

Later, Orrelios and the [[Mandalorian]] rebel [[Sabine Wren]] undertook a [[Mission to Thune City|mission]] to [[Thune City]] on the Wild Space world of [[Thune]] to recover cargo containers and ships on behalf of the rebellion. During their mission, the two came into conflict with the criminal [[Garbis family]].<ref name="Thune Cargo">{{RebelsMagCite|22|The Thune Cargo}}</ref>

===Era of the New Republic and First Order===
Following the [[Battle of Endor]], the [[pirate]] crew of [[Eleodie Maracavanya]] seized control of the [[Executor-class Star Dreadnought|Super Star Destroyer]] [[Liberty's Misrule|''Annihilator'']]. With an Imperial [[Navy]] [[warship]] under their control, Maracavanya came to be known as the "pirate ruler of Wild Space."<ref name="lifedebt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> In [[5 ABY]],<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]'' to [[5 ABY]].</ref> Maracavanya planned to take advantage of the chaos in the wider galaxy by establishing a criminal empire in Wild Space built around individualism and greed.<ref name="lifedebt" />

While searching for [[Chewbacca]], who had been captured by the Empire, [[Han Solo]] came under attack and lost contact with his wife [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] on the edge of Wild Space. Later, the [[New Republic]] [[pilot]]s [[Norra Wexley]] and [[Wedge Antilles]] traveled to the last known coordinates of Han Solo. They were [[Skirmish near Wild Space|attacked]] by [[Commander]] [[Valent]]'s [[Star Destroyer]] [[Scythe (Star Destroyer)|''Scythe'']], but were rescued by New Republic [[Starship|ships]] led by [[Commodore]] [[Kyrsta Agate]], who had received intelligence about Valent from the mysterious Imperial source known as [[Gallius Rax|the Operator]].<ref name="lifedebt" />

After the end of the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Garazeb Orrelios]] took the former [[Imperial Security Bureau|ISB]] [[agent]] turned Rebel [[spy]] [[Alexsandr Kallus]] aboard an [[EF76 Nebulon-B escort frigate]] to Lira San, where Kallus was welcomed as one of them.<ref name="Family Reunion – & Farewell">{{Rebels|Family Reunion &ndash; and Farewell}}</ref> On [[Morak]], [[Morak Imperial remnants|Imperial remnants]] occupied the planet to rebuild their military forces in a bid to return to their former glory.<ref name="CGttSWG" />

During the [[First Order-Resistance War]], [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] of the [[Resistance]] dispatched two of her agents, [[Finn]] and [[Poe Dameron]], to the frontier of Wild Space on a supply mission. The two became involved in a daring [[train]] heist.<ref name="Previews">[[Hyperspace Stories 3|''Hyperspace Stories'' 3]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Wild Space appeared in several [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] literature and media including ''[[Star Wars: The Old Republic]]'', ''[[Star Wars: Darth Vader and the Ghost Prison]]'', and ''[[The Essential Atlas]]''. The region made its first [[Canon]]ical appearance through the planet [[Teth]] in the [[2008]] animated film ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="TCW movie" />

[[Pablo Hidalgo]] explained in [[Rebels Recon]] that Wild Space lay "outside" the known map of the galaxy (in other words, 'off the edge of the map'). By contrast, the borders of the [[Unknown Regions]] were known and defined on the galactic map but the region remained unexplored.<ref name="Rebels Recon 2.14">{{RebelsRecon|cto9_9qNHZ0|#2.14: Inside "The Call" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-the-call}}</ref> This differs from Legends, where Wild Space is on the edge of the known galaxy while everything beyond the known galaxy is part of the Unknown Regions.<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

